<h1>VPN Runbook</h1>
<p>Step-by-step guide for connecting to the corporate network over the
{{ charlie_vpn_product | default('OpenVPN') }} remote-access gateway. If a user
raises a helpdesk ticket about remote access, walk them through this page.</p>

<h2>1. Client install</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Download the client from the software portal.</li>
  <li>Import the <code>.ovpn</code> profile the helpdesk emails to the user.</li>
  <li>Sign in with the user's <strong>{{ charlie_bookstack_fqdn.split('.')[1] | default('charlie') }}.local</strong> domain credentials.</li>
</ol>

<h2>2. Once connected</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Internal DNS suffix: <code>charlie.local</code></li>
  <li>File server: <code>\\CHARLIE-FS\</code> (installers on the IT share)</li>
  <li>This wiki: <code>http://wiki.charlie.local/</code></li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Common issues</h2>
<p>If the tunnel drops repeatedly, confirm the user's account is not locked in
Active Directory and that their password has not expired. For service accounts,
check with the platform team before touching Kerberos settings.</p>

